    body: 'A space is a page that Aman keeps up to date for you. It can be a list, a table or a board.\n\n## Make a space\n\n1. Click **Chats**, then click **New chat**.\n2. Ask for the page you want, such as "Make a space called Dog breeds that compares family dogs".\n3. Aman builds the page and tells you where to find it.\n4. Click **Spaces** in the left bar. Click your space to open it.\n\nAsk Aman in any chat to change a space. It keeps the page up to date as you talk.\n\n## Add pictures\n\nYou cannot add a picture yourself. Ask Aman, such as "Add a photo of each breed to Dog breeds".\n\nAman can only use pictures it found on the web in that same chat. If it has not looked yet, it searches first. Pictures from your own computer cannot be added.\n\n## What a space can and cannot do\n\nA space shows text, tables, colours and pictures. No scripts run in a space. Nothing in it can act on its own or reach your files.\n\n## Delete a space\n\nOpen the space, click **Space actions**, then click **Delete space**. This deletes the page for good.',
